0. Choose source and installation target directories:

   These instructions assume that you have 'git' installed, along with
   a working set of compilers.  GNU (gfortran/gcc) and Intel
   (ifort/icc) compilers are currently supported.  The installation
   scripts use a variable to indicate which compilers to use:

      $compilers = gnu | intel

   Before compiling and installing the software, it's necessary to
   choose directories to manage the source code and the files to be
   installed.  Note that the installation step is required.  Do not
   install the packages in the same directory as the source code.

   For the purpose of these instructions, we will define the following
   path variables:
      $otsdir = target installation directory for external libraries
      $srcdir = directory to hold the SDPC source code directories
      $prefix = target SDPC installation directory (should
                 be different from $otsdir)

   For example, a reasonable choice might be:
       otsdir = $HOME/tempo/ots
       srcdir = $HOME/tempo/git
       prefix = $HOME/tempo/sdpc
       compilers = intel

1. Install the required external libraries:

   A collection of tar files containing most of the external packages
   required by SDPC components is available from one of the CF
   machines, e,g. mars, in:

        /home/jhouck/tempo/ots_sdpc/tarfiles

   Installation of these packages is automated by a revision-controlled
   Makefile available from a git repository:

      cd $srcdir
      git clone git://vex.cfa.harvard.edu/git/ots_sdpc.git

   The README file in the git repository contains installation
   instructions.

2. Install libtell:

   If you haven't already done so, clone the libtell repository:

      cd $srcdir
      git clone git://vex.cfa.harvard.edu/git/libtell.git

   Unless you have a reason for doing otherwise, you probably want
   to compile the 'master' branch:

      cd libtell
      git checkout master

   The INSTALL file in the git repository contains installation
   instructions.

3. Install the programs in the sdpc repository:

   If you haven't already done so, clone the source code repository:

      cd $srcdir
      git clone git://vex.cfa.harvard.edu/git/sdpc.git

   Unless you have a reason for doing otherwise, you probably want
   to compile the 'devel' branch:

      cd sdpc
      git checkout devel

   To compile and install the current devel branch:

    ./configure --prefix=$prefix \
                --with-compilers=$compilers \
                --with-otsroot=$otsdir/$compilers
    make
    make install

   Note that the configure command line shown above assumes that
   the tell library has been installed in $prefix and that the
   external libraries have been installed in $otsdir/$compilers.
